---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Speaking"
  description="Adrian Lee speaks on community strategy, platform safety, and AI governance. Available for conferences, company offsites, and policy convenings."
>
  <div class="speaking-page" style="padding-top: var(--nav-h);">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Speaking</span></div>
        <h1 class="page-header__title">
          Talks that<br>
          <em>change how rooms think.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="page-header__desc">
          Keynotes and workshops on community strategy, platform safety, and AI governance. 
          Practitioner-grounded, frameworks-first, and tailored to your audience.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: var(--space-6); display: inline-flex;" id="speaking-book-hero">
          Book Adrian for your event →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- KEYNOTE TOPICS -->
    <section class="topics section" aria-labelledby="topics-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Keynote topics</span></div>
        <h2 id="topics-heading">Signature talks</h2>

        <div class="topics__grid">

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-1">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 01</div>
            <h3>The Governance Gap: Why Communities Collapse and AI Systems Fail</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
              <span class="badge badge--ai">AI Governance</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              The same structural governance failures that brought down online communities are 
              now appearing in AI systems. This talk maps the pattern, names the failure modes, 
              and offers a practitioner framework for designing governance that holds.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>45–60 min keynote or 90 min workshop</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>AI/tech conferences, policy convenings, executive leadership events</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>The 5 governance failures common to communities and AI systems</li>
                  <li>A diagnostic framework for identifying governance gaps early</li>
                  <li>Participatory design principles for resilient systems</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-2">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 02</div>
            <h3>Building Communities That Last: From First Member to Thriving Ecosystem</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              A practitioner's journey through a decade of community building across gaming, 
              crypto, and consumer tech. What the first 100 members teach you that no playbook 
              will — and the architecture decisions that make or break communities at scale.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>30–60 min keynote</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>Community practitioner conferences, startup events, product team offsites</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>The 0-to-1 community architecture framework</li>
                  <li>Why most community programs fail in year two</li>
                  <li>Measurement frameworks for community health and business impact</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="topic__card card" id="talk-3">
            <div class="topic__number">Talk 03</div>
            <h3>Moderating at Human Scale: Platform Safety Without Burning People Out</h3>
            <div class="topic__badges">
              <span class="badge badge--ai">Platform Safety</span>
              <span class="badge badge--community">Community</span>
            </div>
            <p>
              Moderation is a human problem, not a technical one. This talk covers the 
              structural design of moderation systems that protect communities while protecting 
              the people doing the moderating — drawing on experience across millions of users.
            </p>
            <div class="topic__details">
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Format</span>
                <span>45 min keynote or half-day workshop</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Best for</span>
                <span>Trust &amp; safety teams, platform operators, policy audiences</span>
              </div>
              <div class="topic__detail">
                <span class="label">Key takeaways</span>
                <ul>
                  <li>Tiered moderation architecture that scales without proportional headcount</li>
                  <li>Moderator wellbeing frameworks and burn-out prevention</li>
                  <li>Metrics for moderation system health</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SPEAKING LOGISTICS -->
    <section class="logistics section--sm" aria-labelledby="logistics-heading">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Before you book</span></div>
        <h2 id="logistics-heading">What to expect</h2>

        <div class="logistics__grid">
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">📍</span>
            <h3>Travel</h3>
            <p>Based in Singapore. Available for events across Asia Pacific. International travel considered for the right events — please enquire.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">🎯</span>
            <h3>Customization</h3>
            <p>All talks are tailored to the specific audience, context, and desired outcomes. I'll spend time understanding your event before agreeing to speak.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">📅</span>
            <h3>Availability</h3>
            <p>Book at least 4–6 weeks in advance for keynotes. 8+ weeks for workshops or events requiring significant customization.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="logistics__item">
            <span class="logistics__icon">💬</span>
            <h3>What I need from you</h3>
            <p>Event name, date, format, expected audience size and background, and what you want the audience to walk away thinking or doing differently.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SPEAKING CTA -->
    <section class="speaking-cta section--sm" aria-labelledby="speaking-cta-heading">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="card card--featured speaking-cta__card">
          <h2 id="speaking-cta-heading">Book Adrian for your event</h2>
          <p>Send the details of your event and I'll get back to you within 48 hours with availability and next steps.</p>
          <a href="/contact?type=speaking" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" id="speaking-book-cta">Send speaking enquiry →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* TOPICS */
.topics h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.topics__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); }
.topic__card { padding: var(--space-8); }
.topic__number { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--terracotta); letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.topic__card h3 { font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.topic__badges { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
.topic__card > p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
.topic__details { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4); background: var(--bg-elevated); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-6); }
.topic__detail { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 100px 1fr; gap: var(--space-4); }
.topic__detail .label { font-size: 0.7rem; padding-top: 2px; }
.topic__detail span:last-child { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
.topic__detail ul { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
.topic__detail li::before { content: '→ '; color: var(--terracotta); }
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .topic__detail { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-2); }
}

/* LOGISTICS */
.logistics h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.logistics__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-5); }
.logistics__item { padding: var(--space-6); background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
.logistics__icon { font-size: 1.5rem; display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.logistics__item h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.logistics__item p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
@media (max-width: 600px) { .logistics__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

/* CTA */
.speaking-cta__card { padding: var(--space-10); text-align: center; }
.speaking-cta__card h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.speaking-cta__card > p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); max-width: 440px; margin-inline: auto; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
</style>
